    "id": "dvb-t2-bit-interleave-baselines",
    "issue": "eda07788",
    "purpose": "consumer-family",
    "description": "Confirmatory comparator-gap baselines for the DVB-T2 ETSI EN 302 755 v1.4.1 SS6.1.3 bit interleaver (parity interleaving composed with column twisting), Rate 1/2 Normal FECFRAME, N=64800. Six whole-consumer cells: two MODCODs crossed with three comparisons. Every cell's baseline arm is the established gf2 implementation and every candidate arm is the arm whose lead would need attribution, so the speedup of medians is median(gf2)/median(candidate) and a value above 1 means the candidate is ahead. In a `-gap-` cell the candidate is the xdsopl/LDPC PCTITL comparator, so `improved` would mean a material gap in the comparator's favour and `regressed` means gf2 is materially ahead of it; in a `-control-` cell the candidate is the `-C target-cpu=native` gf2 build and the baseline is the conservative-portable scalar/compiler control, so the cell asks what the architecture level buys for this operation. This issue is a baseline survey: it proposes no production adoption, so no cell here selects a production candidate and the receipt is not expected to qualify."
  },
