    },
    "equivalence_margin": 1.1,
    "equivalence_rationale": "A 10% equivalence margin. The pilot's largest relative confidence-interval half-width over its ten cells is 0.055, so 0.10 lies outside the measured resolution; restricted to the six cells this family measures the largest is 0.0245, so the margin is conservative twice over. It is tight enough that the two control cells, whose pilot estimates sit on 1.00, can still be declared not worse rather than inconclusive.",
    "material_gap_threshold": 1.2,
    "material_gap_rationale": "A 20% whole-consumer wall-clock gap is the smallest gap between two arms of this operation worth attributing to a named cause (representation conversion, permutation-table traffic, or codegen level) rather than to host noise on this shared eight-worker machine. It sits above the pilot-measured resolution of 0.06 by more than a factor of three, so a cell that resolves at this threshold resolves on evidence rather than on noise."
